ith no lag for a second or so then it lags for a good 5 seconds on my end then it's back. I am currently converting back to 4.6.3.stable, because there's a different issue I faced. I installed Terrain3D from the Asset Store and I would do basic operations like creating a Terrain3D node and adding a region and it would crash then be okay the crash until it crashes again for a completely separate operation, which is unusual for every other time I used Terrain3D. I experienced a similar thing with a different plugin still on 4.7.(1?).stable, I don't remember which plugin it was but I brushed it off as the plugin being wrong. I was in the process of coding a component-based player system when I figured out the 5 second lag-spike situation, I ignored it hoping it would go away but nah, then I thought surely I am doing something wrong with @tool scripts. I may open a different issue regarding 4.7.2.stable's stability if I see that the same code I am trying to get working is fine on 4.6.3.stable. A bit of dump of information here I know, hope it helps diagnose some issue(s) in some way.\n\nEdit: Terrain3D off the asset library does crash on 4.6.3.stable when I go and save it*","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5714974546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5823235092","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122229#issuecomment-5823235092","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122229","id":5823235092,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWxeEFA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://git